---
/* =============================================================================
   The homepage — one implementation, two languages
   =============================================================================
   Both `/` and `/ar/` render this. The alternative — two 300-line page files —
   guarantees they drift apart, and a drifted Arabic homepage is exactly the
   "visual afterthought" §10 forbids.

   ── THE FROZEN ORDER (Website Structure v2, 2026-08-17) ─────────────────────

     1. Hero                          I ❤ Tech
     2. What I'm Exploring Now        Building · Testing · Learning
     3. Vibe Coding                   building with AI
     4. Gear                          using and testing technology
     5. Learn                         the gateway to the library
     6. Playground                    what you can actually open
     7. Latest                        real published content, or nothing
     8. About + Newsletter            the close
     9. Footer                        (Base.astro)

   Two sections joined the IA v2.0 order that preceded this file: the
   orientation trio at §2, and Latest at §7.

   §2 answers the question a first-time visitor actually arrives with — "what
   is this person doing right now" — before the page starts arguing for
   individual pillars. Three doors, named, one screen.

   §7 sits after everything the reader can DO and before the personal close,
   because a feed is the least opinionated thing on the page and the close
   should still be last. It renders published content or it renders nothing:
   with fewer than two real items it is absent from the DOM entirely.

   ── EVERY SECTION COLLAPSES ON ITS OWN ──────────────────────────────────────
   §3 and §4 are gated on real assets (a build needs a real screenshot, a gear
   story needs a real photograph), §5 drops any surface with nothing published,
   §6 lists only tools you can actually open, §7 disappears below two items.
   §2 never collapses — it is navigation, and all three destinations have
   designed empty states of their own.

   With an empty content directory this page is a hero, three doors, four honest
   lines and a close — which is the correct state, not a broken one.

   CS-05: exactly one primary action on this page, and it is the hero's. Every
   other action below is secondary, ghost or a plain link.
   ========================================================================== */

import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../home/Hero.astro';
import Exploring from '../home/Exploring.astro';
import RealWorld from '../home/RealWorld.astro';
import GearSection from '../home/GearSection.astro';
import LearnSection from '../home/LearnSection.astro';
import PlaygroundSection from '../home/PlaygroundSection.astro';
import Latest from '../home/Latest.astro';
import AboutSubscribe from '../home/AboutSubscribe.astro';
import { site } from '../../site.config';
import type { Lang } from '../../i18n';

interface Props {
  lang: Lang;
}

const { lang } = Astro.props;

const description = lang === 'ar' ? site.descriptionAr : site.description;
---

<Base lang={lang} padded={false} description={description}>
  {/* 1 — Hero. I ❤ Tech. */}
  <Hero lang={lang} />

  {/* 2 — What I'm exploring now. Three doors: Building, Testing, Learning. */}
  <Exploring lang={lang} />

  {/* 3 — Vibe Coding in the Real World. Building with AI. */}
  <RealWorld lang={lang} />

  {/* 4 — Gear. Using and testing technology. */}
  <GearSection lang={lang} />

  {/* 5 — Learn. The gateway to the library, not the library. */}
  <LearnSection lang={lang} />

  {/* 6 — Playground. Only what you can actually open. */}
  <PlaygroundSection lang={lang} />

  {/* 7 — Latest. Real published content, or nothing at all. */}
  <Latest lang={lang} />

  {/* 8 — About + Subscribe. The close. */}
  <AboutSubscribe lang={lang} />

  {/* 9 — Footer, from Base.astro. */}
</Base>
